Completion HUD works, but toast "ARMA MATERIALIZADA • RARO" overlaps the tracker's progress bar. Since onWeapon shows toast at top 18%, again overlapping. This is cosmetic and temporary (2.9s). But user sees overlap. Better shift toast down when harvest HUD visible, or remove toast for weapon completion (HUD complete shows). We could reposition toast globally to top 24%? It already overlapped at top 18% (~138px) with tracker 94-190. Toast is centered in tracker. Better adjustment: when harvest HUD visible, add class to body or toast `harvest-toast` that positions it below tracker. Simpler: in `onWeapon`, if `!els.harvestHud.classList.contains('is-hidden')` (i.e., complete HUD), skip toast? The completion HUD itself announces. But onWeapon is also called for default start with animate false. For materialization, if harvest HUD visible, skip toast. Let's implement:
```
if (animate) {
 ...
 if (els.harvestHud.classList.contains('is-hidden')) showToast(...);
 ...
}
```
But the harvest HUD at that moment: in finishHarvest, setWeapon is called before onHarvestComplete. At that point the harvest HUD is still visible from progress (class no complete). So skip toast. Then onHarvestComplete shows complete HUD for 1.9s. Great. This avoids duplicate. If forging instant (mode not playing or options.instant) and HUD hidden → toast shows. Good.

Apply.

